From 4f7084de88e99c8654ab9d9e6e52fe95e3eeb4f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:20:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/36] Preserve undefined lane definitions in identity copies

Reuse the prepared 0028 extraction as a compiler prerequisite. The
far-word boundary workload reaches its existing identity-copy lane
contract in word_pressure. The missing-patch compiler and pre-rewriter
MIR are retained; this is reconciliation of an existing root repair.

Pristine destination still removes the allocated identity copy without
remembering its undef-lane definition. Preserve the current
readsUndefSubreg(MI, MO) interface and the prepared generic X86 regression.

The change is kept minimal (independent review N2): copyHasUndefLanes()
decides, before an instruction's operands are rewritten, whether a COPY's
source has lanes that are not live there, and handleIdentityCopy() keeps
such an identity copy as a KILL. The rewrite loop is otherwise unchanged.
virtregrewriter-x86-undef-high-byte-result.mir is the regression test;
virtregrewriter-x86-copy-contracts.mir characterizes the existing
identity-copy contracts and passes without this change, as its header says.
This generic VirtRegMap.cpp change needs its own llvm-project path or an
explicit llvm-mos carry decision.

Default-mode effect: unchanged from the reviewed patch. Outside the
changes below the fixed input set is identical on every MOS CPU except
mosspc700, which crashes in MOS Late Optimizations before and after;
fixed separately by #584. On the fixed input set, examples_snes_bf-vm changes on every MOS CPU except mosspc700 and
mossweet16 (+8 bytes of .text on mos6502, mos65c02 and mosw65816: a kept
lane definition becomes a register copy before two pair spills), and
examples_snes_metaball (+1 byte) and examples_snes_sodo (+8 bytes) change
on mosw65816.

Prior extraction: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.0 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra,
xhigh reasoning effort; session 01a0db16-f6a0-7e32-ada6-0c8098813933.
Prior independent review: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1, model gpt-6-astra,
xhigh reasoning effort; session 01a0db96-a6cd-7800-82a5-6b871eb7e177.
Reapplication and validation: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (session source
vscode), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session
01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84. Earlier implementation credits
remain in the canonical mos-coalescing-rc-undef record.

Minimal form and test labels (review N2): Claude Code 2.1.285 (t4-opus-high agent), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort.

